  {
    "title": "Curtain: Poirot's Last Case",
    "type": "Novel",
    "character": "Hercule Poirot",
    "year": 1975,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/curtain-poirots-last-case",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/hcus-paperback/Jacket_USCurtain.jpg",
    "synopsis": "Poirot and Hastings come full circle at Styles, and there is still one case for Poirot to solve. Who is the serial killer X?",
    "moreAbout": "Arthritic and immobilized, Poirot calls on his old friend Captain Hastings to join him at Styles to be the eyes and ears that will feed observations to Poirot's still razor sharp mind. Though aware of the criminal's identity, Poirot will not reveal it to the frustrated Hastings, and dubs the nameless personage 'X'. Already responsible for several murders, X, Poirot warns, is ready to strike again, and the partners must work swiftly to prevent imminent murder.\n\nPoirot’s final case, a mystery which brings him and Hastings back to Styles where they first solved a crime together.\n\nAgatha Christie wrote it during World War II, as a gift for her daughter should she not survive the bombings, and it was kept in a safe for over thirty years. It was agreed among the family that Curtain would be published finally in 1975 by Collins, her long-standing publishers, and that Sleeping Murder (the Marple story written during the war for her husband, Max) would follow.",
    "trivia": [],
    "quote": null,
    "extractPdf": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/image-store/Read-Christie-2024/ACL_PoirotList_2024.pdf",
    "related": [
      {
        "title": "The Mysterious Affair at Styles",
        "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/the-mysterious-affair-at-styles"
      },
      {
        "title": "The Murder of Roger Ackroyd",
