  {
    "title": "The Mysterious Mr Quin",
    "type": "Collection",
    "character": "Harley Quin",
    "year": 1930,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/the-myserious-mr-quin",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/hcuk-paperback/The-Mysterious-Mr-Quin-US.jpg",
    "synopsis": "It had been a typical New Year’s Eve party. But as midnight approaches, Mr Satterthwaite - ­­a keen observer of human nature – senses that the real drama of the evening is yet to unfold. And so it proves when a mysterious stranger knocks on the door. Who is Mr Quin?\n\nMr Satterthwaite’s new friend is an enigma. Throughout this collection of short stories he seems to appear and disappear almost like a trick of the light. In fact, the only consistent thing about him is that his presence is always an omen – sometimes good, but sometimes deadly.",
    "moreAbout": null,
    "trivia": [
      "The Mysterious Mr Quin book dedication reads ‘To Harlequin the invisible.’ This is the only time that Christie dedicated a book to one of her fictional characters.",
      "Agatha Christie’s favourite Mr Quin stories were World’s End, The Man from the Sea and Harlequin’s Lane."
    ],
    "quote": {
      "text": "Mr Satterthwaite watched the drama unfold before his eyes. Quietly and naturally, Mr Quin was pulling the strings, setting his puppets in motion.",
      "author": "Agatha Christie, The Coming of Mr Quin"
    },
    "extractPdf": null,
