  {
    "title": "Parker Pyne Investigates",
    "type": "Collection",
    "character": "Parker Pyne",
    "year": 1934,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/parker-pyne-investigates",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/hcus-paperback/Parker-Pyne-Investigates.jpg",
    "synopsis": "Mrs Packington felt alone, helpless and utterly forlorn. But her life changed when she stumbled upon an advertisement in The Times which read: ‘Are you happy? If not, consult Mr Parker Pyne.'\n\nParker Pyne is a most unconventional investigator. In a uniquely charming way, he solves matters of the heart, yearnings for adventure, and one or two crimes along the way.\n\nThis collection comprises fourteen tantalising cases for this intriguing retired civil servant.",
    "moreAbout": null,
    "trivia": [],
