  {
    "title": "And Then There Were None - Play",
    "type": "Play",
    "character": null,
    "year": 1943,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/and-then-there-were-none-play",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/image-store/Plays/Jacket_AndThenThereWereNone_Play.jpg",
    "synopsis": "Ten strangers are trapped on an island. One by one, they are accused of murder. One by one, they start to die.",
    "moreAbout": "Ten strangers are summoned to a remote island. All that the guests have in common is a wicked past they're unwilling to reveal and a secret that will seal their fate. For each has been marked for murder. As the weather turns and the group is cut off from the mainland, the bloodbath begins and one by one they are brutally murdered in accordance with the lines of a sinister nursery rhyme.\n\nThe play was adapted by Agatha Christie based on one of her darkest and most successful novels, And Then There Were None. In writing the stage version, Christie responded to the mood of the times by introducing a more positive ending. The play is now available with this ending and with an alternative ending, drawn from the novel and using entirely Agatha Christie's own words.",
    "trivia": [],
    "quote": null,
    "extractPdf": null,
    "related": [
      {
