  {
    "title": "The Case of the City Clerk",
    "type": "Short Story",
    "character": "Parker Pyne",
    "year": 1932,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/the-case-of-the-city-clerk",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/hcus-paperback/Parker-Pyne-Investigates.jpg",
    "synopsis": "With his family on holiday, the conventional Mr Roberts goes to Parker Pyne seeking to inject excitement into his drab life. Before long Roberts finds more romance and intrigue than he’d bargained for.",
    "moreAbout": "Mr Roberts has lived contently, is happily married and has a steady job. Tired of the humdrum nature of his days, he longs for adventure and it is Parker Pyne who assists.\n\nIn this story Parker Pyne once again makes use of his beautiful assistant, Madeleine de Sara. However, this creature, whom Pyne has referred to as the “Queen of the Vamps”, is not everything she seems; better known to her family as Maggie Sayers, she is the fourth daughter of an honest hard-working family living in Streatham, South London.\n\nThis story first appeared in the US in Cosmopolitan magazine, and later in the 1934 collection of short stories Parker Pyne Investigates.\n\nIt has never been adapted.",
    "trivia": [],
    "quote": null,
    "extractPdf": null,
