  {
    "title": "Have You Got Everything You Want?",
    "type": "Short Story",
    "character": "Parker Pyne",
    "year": 1933,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/have-you-got-everything-you-want",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/hcus-paperback/Parker-Pyne-Investigates.jpg",
    "synopsis": "Boarding the Orient Express at the Gare de Lyon, a young woman discovers the presence of the detective Parker Pyne on the train, who is there to solve a jewel robbery that hasn’t happened yet. She thinks she might know the intended victim…",
    "moreAbout": "An attractive young wife boards the Orient Express where she chances upon Parker Pyne. She admits she is unhappy and that her husband has left a cryptic message which involves her in some way.\n\nParker Pyne again follows in the footsteps of Hercule Poirot. Both men travelled down the Nile and encountered murder and both men travel on the Orient Express, meeting people in crisis, both this story and Murder on the Orient Express being published in the same year. They also shared a working friendship with Ariadne Oliver, the crime novelist through which Agatha Christie voiced many of her views, and Poirot's secretary Miss Lemon originally worked for Parker Pyne.\n\nThis story first appeared in the US in Cosmopolitan magazine, and later in the collection of short stories, Parker Pyne Investigates.\n\nIt has never been adapted.",
    "trivia": [],
    "quote": null,
    "extractPdf": null,
    "related": [
      {
        "title": "The Regatta Mystery",
