  {
    "title": "The Strange Case of Sir Arthur Carmichael",
    "type": "Short Story",
    "character": null,
    "year": 1933,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/the-strange-case-of-sir-arthur-carmichael",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/hcus-paperback/Jacket_USLastSeance.jpg",
    "synopsis": "A man takes on the habits of a cat but only his psychologist seems able to see a real cat in the house. In The Hound of Death and The Golden Ball and Other Stories.",
    "moreAbout": "Classic country house Agatha Christie, except for the small fact that the gentlemen in question has not been murdered, but appears instead to have become a cat.The story was first published in book form in the UK in the Oldhams Press edition of The House of Death in 1933, available only by collecting coupons from a magazine entitled The Passing Show. It was first published in the US in the 1971 collection The Golden Ball and Other Stories.\n\nIt has never been adapted.",
