      },
      {
        "title": "A Murder is Announced",
        "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/a-murder-is-announced"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "The Case of the Perfect Maid",
    "type": "Short Story",
    "character": "Miss Marple",
    "year": 1942,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/the-case-of-the-perfect-maid",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/image-store/Jacket_MissMarpleTheCompleteShortStories_US.jpg",
    "synopsis": "A maid is sacked for theft, but when Miss Marple's maid says that her replacement is still stealing from her employers, the elderly sleuth suspects something is not quite right... From Three Blind Mice and Other Stories and Miss Marple's Final Cases.",
    "moreAbout": "Miss Marple knows a thing or two about maids and her interest is immediately piqued when the Skinner sisters sack one for theft and replace her only to find that the items keep on disappearing. Strange behaviour indeed...\n\nOnce again Miss Marple comes to the aid of Inspector Slack in this story originally published in 1942 (UK). In Strand Magazine it was titled The Perfect Maid and in Chicago Sunday Tribune it was called The Maid Who Disappeared. It was included in the collections Three Blind Mice and Other Stories (US) in 1950 and later in Miss Marple's Final Cases (UK) in 1979.\n\nIt was also adapted for Japanese TV in the anime series Agatha Christie's Great Detectives in 2004, which had Poirot meeting Miss Marple's great niece and solving crimes together. The episode was called The Faultless Maid.",
    "trivia": [],
    "quote": null,
    "extractPdf": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/image-store/Read-Christie-2024/ACL_MarpleList_2024.pdf",
