      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "The Dressmaker's Doll",
    "type": "Short Story",
    "character": null,
    "year": 1958,
    "url": "https://www.agathachristie.com/stories/the-dressmakers-doll",
    "cover": "https://agathachristie.imgix.net/image-store/double_sin_PB.jpg",
    "synopsis": "A doll appears in a dressmaker's shop, a floppy, long-legged doll who sits itself on the best sofa. But where did it come from and why does it appear to watch everyone? From Miss Marple's Final Cases and Double Sin and Other Stories.",
    "moreAbout": "Alicia Coombe manages her very smart dressmaking business with the help of her young assistant, Sybil. One day, a doll appears in the shop, a floppy, long-legged doll who sits itself on the best sofa. But where did it come from and why does it appear to watch them?\n\nA creepy tale from Agatha Christie, in which she indulges in her fascination with the supernatural, it was first published in Woman’s Journal in 1958. Although it appeared in Miss Marple’s Final Cases in the UK (1979) it is not a Marple story. It can also be found in Double Sin and Other Stories in the US (1961).",
    "trivia": [],
    "quote": null,
    "extractPdf": null,
